cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PulseCraft PPG, an open photoplethysmography kit"
message: "If you use PulseCraft PPG for teaching, research, workshops, or a derivative kit, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chierico
    given-names: Pietro
    email: pietrochr@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Universitat Politecnica de Valencia (visiting PhD at Khalifa University)"
year: 2026
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PietroChierico/PulseCraft-PPG"
url: "https://PietroChierico.github.io/PulseCraft-PPG/"
abstract: >-
  A project-based educational kit for photoplethysmography (PPG). It contains Arduino and
  ESP32 acquisition firmware, a 3D-printable MAX3010x sensor enclosure, Python pipelines for
  guided data collection, filtering and feature extraction, small interpretable machine-learning
  models, real-time GUI demonstrations, and a synthetic-signal simulator that lets every wireless
  project run without hardware. Five projects cover physical-activity recognition, caffeine
  response, relaxation biofeedback, a voluntary-apnea SpO2 proxy, and live mental-stress
  detection. Built for the Khalifa University CMHS Summer Internship Program 2026.
